 ## Overview
-Hybrid Regularization and Training Strategy is a two-stage optimization method for voxel-based neural radiance fields that mitigates overfitting in explicit feature grids by leveraging an implicit neural network for initialization [S1, S2]. It solves the problem of deterministic integration prone to overfitting at specific voxels when features are directly optimized, which leads to degenerate solutions like floaters or holes in sparse input scenarios [S1, S2]. It sets itself apart from pure explicit regularization by using an intermediate implicit phase to provide a powerful initialization, and from pure implicit methods by discarding the network to allow direct grid optimization for higher final quality [S1, S2].
+Hybrid Regularization and Training Strategy is a two-stage optimization method for voxel-based neural radiance fields that mitigates overfitting in explicit feature grids by leveraging an implicit neural network for initialization [S1, S2]. It solves the problem of deterministic integration being prone to overfitting at specific voxels when features are directly optimized, which leads to degenerate solutions like floaters or holes in sparse input scenarios [S1, S2]. It sets itself apart from pure explicit regularization by using an intermediate implicit phase to provide a powerful initialization, and from pure implicit methods by discarding the network to allow direct grid optimization for higher final quality [S1, S2].
 
